From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:28:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: A80: enable the timestamp counter in U-Boot proper

The A80 timestamp generator drives the generic timer counter. The SPL
enables it, but on some cold boots the enable does not stick: the counter
stays at 0, and Linux hangs at the first delay ("smp: Bringing up
secondary CPUs"). Enable it again in board_init().

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/cpu_sun9i.h | 2 ++
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/clock_sun9i.c           | 2 +-
 board/sunxi/board.c                         | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/cpu_sun9i.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/cpu_sun9i.h
index 73de4707c1..d583f622e6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/cpu_sun9i.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/cpu_sun9i.h
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@
 
 #define SUNXI_GIC400_BASE		(REGS_AHB0_BASE + 0x40000)
 
+#define SUNXI_TIMESTAMP_BASE		0x01720000
+
 #define SUNXI_DRAM_COM_BASE		(REGS_AHB0_BASE + 0x62000)
 #define SUNXI_DRAM_CTL0_BASE		(REGS_AHB0_BASE + 0x63000)
 #define SUNXI_DRAM_CTL1_BASE		(REGS_AHB0_BASE + 0x64000)
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/clock_sun9i.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/clock_sun9i.c
index 5f99071f21..245a46ec75 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/clock_sun9i.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/clock_sun9i.c
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ void clock_init_safe(void)
 	setbits_le32(&ccm->apb1_gate, (1 << 24));
 
 	/* set enable-bit in TSTAMP_CTRL_REG */
-	writel(1, 0x01720000);
+	writel(1, SUNXI_TIMESTAMP_BASE);
 }
 
 void clock_init_uart(void)
diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 3d1afec7c6..cac2832599 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -203,6 +203,15 @@ int board_init(void)
 	if ((id_pfr1 >> CPUID_ARM_GENTIMER_SHIFT) & 0xf) {
 		uint32_t freq;
 
+		/*
+		 * The A80 timestamp generator drives the generic timer counter.
+		 * The SPL enables it, but the enable does not always stick on a
+		 * cold boot. Then the counter stays at 0 and Linux hangs at the
+		 * first delay. Enable it again.
+		 */
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN9I))
+			writel(1, SUNXI_TIMESTAMP_BASE);
+
 		debug("Setting CNTFRQ\n");
 
 		/*
-- 
